{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"2026 error-detection research returned. KEY FINDINGS vs our design. (1) CONFIRMS the diagnosis with a 2023 citation: RARR (Gao et al., ACL 2023) documented this exact bug - 'RARR currently does not try to modify subsequent reasoning steps which may no longer be logically entailed', plus footnote 'attribution does not entail correctness'. Our citation veto is an ATTRIBUTION gate; attribution gates provably do not catch invalid inference. (2) CONTRADICTS a fixed design decision: the Phase-3 convergence rule (same_approach OR same_end_state) is actively contraindicated by tier-(a) replicated evidence - Huang et al. show debate underperforms self-consistency at matched compute; the 2026 conformity wave measures 85.5% modal adoption, 70% vulnerability, and 57-77% of conformity being correct-to-wrong; Pan et al. name the 'consensus trap'; Wang and Yang show answer-level consensus does not entail reasoning-level alignment. Agreement between proposers is close to no evidence under shared priors. (3) NEW, cheapest high-value change - PRE-COMMITMENT/de-anchoring: Zhou arXiv:2607.05904 finds 'conditioned on a candidate, a judge scores plausibility, not correctness' and that committing an answer first drops judge false-positive rate 0.719 to 0.012. We have blindness but NOT pre-commitment. (4) QUALIFIES the approved intent check: 'retrieved the right record' and 'acted on it' are separately-failing capabilities - STALE 55.2%, MemoryAgentBench <=28% multi-hop even when handed the ordering rule. The hardest case, triangulated across three unrelated literatures, is IMPLICIT conflict where a later decision invalidates an earlier one without explicit negation - which is exactly the item-16 shape (ed13 replaced free-text with a bounded class rather than negating anything). Implication: the intent check must SURFACE the record, not adjudicate it. (5) SUPPORTS the basis-field rejection: knowing-saying gap - internal representations discriminate correctness at 0.92-0.99 AUROC while verbalized confidence sits at 0.50-0.63; Advani finds TF-IDF detectors beat LLM judges at spotting agent overclaiming (0.83/0.95 vs 0.65/0.54). Caveat: the specific executed/read/inferred variant is UNTESTED rather than disproven."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786058005678970001,"uuid":"c89eea51-15e4-411f-8c78-703ac18fd188"}